name: use-github-actions
'on':
- push",
  "rationale": "The workflow repeatedly fetches and installs Perl dependencies via cpanm into ~/perl_modules on every run across both jobs, with CI history showing repeated successful push runs. The P-LIT-GHA-CACHE pattern (dependency_cache) supports caching dependency downloads to reduce repeated fetch/install time while keeping all installation and test steps intact. Adding actions/cache@v4 for ~/perl_modules before the cpanm steps preserves full build and test coverage, uses only the writable user directory (no privileged access or new network endpoints), and introduces no unrelated changes. A versioned cache key with restore keys is used since no dependency lockfile exists in the repository.",
  "evidence_ids": ["pattern:P-LIT-GHA-CACHE"]
}
